events.intro:
{rival} is in the road, turning out their bag onto the stones. Berries, Balls, a map, a broken clasp. They don't pretend to be fine.

{say ace-missing||bitter-challenger::"It's not stolen. I checked. It left." They don't look up.||prodigy::"It isn't stolen. I checked everywhere. It *left*." They say it like a ruling, and the ruling hurts.||enthusiast::"It's not stolen! I checked. It, um. It left." The grin they try for doesn't hold.||idealist::"It's not stolen. I checked. It left. I think it had a reason, and I don't know the reason."||strategist::"It's not stolen. I checked. It left. I have no theory for that, and I always have a theory."||protector::"It's not stolen. I checked. It left. I should have seen it coming. I always see it coming."||underdog::"It's not stolen. I checked. It left. Everyone leaves, sooner or later. I just thought it was different."||champion-chaser::"It's not stolen. I checked. It left. A champion's ace doesn't leave. So what does that make me?"}

*Some rivals can't ask. Those ones just stand there. They are standing there now, and they are not asking.*
